  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` passes (7 of 7).\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a rejected job never decremented `running` and never started the next job. Now success and failure both go through the same cleanup step, which frees the slot, starts the next job and checks for idle. A job that throws synchronously, or returns a plain value, is also handled now. Before, `fn().then` would throw on it and leave the counts wrong.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving early:** it only checked that nothing was pending. It now also requires `running === 0`.\n- **Only one job after `pause()`/`resume()`:** `next()` started at most one job per call. It now loops until the concurrency limit is reached or nothing is left to start, so `resume()` fills every free slot.\n\nI added five regression tests to `test/queue.test.js`:\n- a failing job rejects only itself and the queue keeps going;\n- synchronous throws and plain return values;\n- `onIdle()` waits for running jobs, and resolves immediately when idle;\n- `onIdle()` also resolves after a failing job;\n- `resume()` fills all four slots with concurrency 4.\n\nWhile the queue is paused with jobs still pending, `onIdle()` stays unresolved. The contract says idle means nothing pending and nothing running, so I kept that.",
